cosmic-comp: opt-in control of the NVIDIA "dithering mode" connector property.

The NVIDIA driver exposes "dithering mode" (auto, off, static 2x2, dynamic 2x2,
temporal, on) instead of "max bpc", and cosmic-comp never sets it; temporal
dithering can make some panels flicker on certain colours.  When an output is
set up, set it from COSMIC_DRM_DITHERING_<CONNECTOR> (e.g.
COSMIC_DRM_DITHERING_DP_2=off for DP-2) or else COSMIC_DRM_DITHERING.  Nothing
changes when neither is set or the connector lacks the property.

